# CareFlow: Clinical Pathway Process Mining

## 1. Project Overview

**Project Name:** CareFlow – Clinical Pathway Process Mining  
**Domain:** Healthcare Operations and Process Analytics  
**Project Type:** Data Engineering, Process Mining and Business Intelligence

CareFlow is a healthcare process analytics project that analyses hospital patient journeys using Electronic Health Record (EHR) event logs. It aims to identify delays, repeated activities and bottlenecks in hospital workflows.

The project uses Python, data processing and process mining techniques to understand how patients move between hospital departments and help administrators identify areas for improvement.

## 2. Problem Statement

Hospital administrators often know the average patient waiting time, but they may not know exactly where delays happen.

Traditional dashboards show summary information but cannot always explain the actual sequence of patient activities.

CareFlow aims to analyse patient journeys and identify process delays and repeated activities.

## 3. Project Objectives

- Generate simulated hospital event log data.
- Prepare and clean the event log data.
- Understand patient movement through hospital departments.
- Identify repeated activities and process bottlenecks.
- Calculate elapsed time between consecutive activities.
- Develop a Power BI dashboard to visualise the analysis.
- Support better understanding of hospital workflows.

## 4. Technologies and Tools Used

| Tool | Purpose |
|---|---|
| Python | Generate and process hospital event data |
| Pandas | Data cleaning and analysis |
| DuckDB | Local data storage and querying |
| PM4Py | Process mining and event log analysis |
| CSV | Store and exchange event log data |
